# Suppressions for reachable memory held by the glibc dynamic linker (ld.so)
# when libcurl lazily loads its SSL/TLS backend via dlopen(3).
#
# These blocks are owned by ld.so's internal bookkeeping (link_map structs,
# library path strings, symbol-version hash tables) and are intentionally kept
# live until process exit.  They cannot be freed from application code even
# with a correct curl_global_cleanup() call.  They are not leaks.
#
# Two suppressions cover all variants because the allocations go through either
# malloc (for link_map structs and strdup'd path strings) or calloc (for
# _dl_new_object and _dl_check_map_versions tables), with _dl_open always
# present somewhere in the call chain above them.

{
   ld_so_dlopen_reachable_malloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:_dl_open
}

{
   ld_so_dlopen_reachable_calloc
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:calloc
   ...
   fun:_dl_open
}
